Changes, November 2026: the C++ model (P.528, and the parts of P.676 and P.835 it calls) is translated to Rust. The
computation of every loss NTIA's software returns is unchanged. The differences:

- Inputs and results are Rust types; errors are a Rust enum carrying NTIA's return codes.
- Where NTIA's software returns success with a value that is not a loss, this software returns an error: NaN when the
  path leaves the reference atmosphere (NTIA's atmosphere functions return their error codes as values), 0 dB for
  terminals at the same height and 0 km apart (NTIA's code 10), and NaN for an input that is NaN or an infinite
  distance.
- The work that does not depend on the distance or the time percentage can be done once for many distances; the
  gaseous properties of the layers between the two terminals are stored and reused. The arithmetic is the same.
- Two bisection loops return once their step reaches zero, where NTIA's loop would not end; this changes no result
  that NTIA's software returns.

The files under reference/ntia-p528/ntia are NTIA's, unmodified. They are used only by this crate's tests.
